# HG2-B (ROOT5V, data(D)): D is a Structure of the data part of main. `data(D)` is `call(D data)` (#ordinary-var,
# #data-code-roles). The declaration `int: n 5` of the data record, run over D, assigns the existing place of D's n,
# which is the call's local (#call-frame-20261115): D\n keeps the value declared in D (1); the explicit write data\n := 9
# is f's own data. The published value 9 is not kept by the norm: observed seen 1 (values-changed).
(
    Observed:
        int: r 0
        int: seen 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: f () int (int: n 5)
    data\n := 9
    data(D)
    return: 1
sub: main () (
    D(int: n 1)
    int: r 0
    int: seen 0
)
    data\r := f()
    data\seen := D\n
    shared\Observed\r := data\r
    shared\Observed\seen := data\seen
main()
